 "notes": "The iron steamer Lina (70 x 9 m, 1879) upright on the slope off Cape Pecenj, Cres, bow up the slope at 25 m towards the shore and stern at 55 m. Position from pro-taucher.com (taken as the bow buoy), shoreline from OpenStreetMap, dimensions, bow buoy, standing bow mast, timber cargo in the holds, bridge at 40 m and the usual route from krnicadive.com; the funnel with its '6' and its chains from first-hand observation. The heading is not published: the hull is drawn straight down the slope (bow NE, perpendicular to the coast), and positions along the hull are approximate. EMODnet bathymetry places the coast west-facing here.",
